# TOPAS 3000A — Python AsyncAPI Client

Generated SDK and runnable scenario snippets for consuming TOPAS 3000A
AMQP 1.0 messages from Python.

## Layout

- `sdk/` — typed message classes generated by Modelina from `asyncapi.yaml`.
- `snippets/s1.py` — subscribe to `{{ channels.detector_measurement }}` and print messages.
- `snippets/s2.py` — subscribe to `{{ channels.wildcard_fault }}` (all faults across all domains; A8).
- `snippets/s3.py` — publish a VMS DisplayMessage and await the correlated response (A4 + A6).
- `snippets/s4.py` — distinguish sync vs delta messages and detect sync-batch completion (A3 + A5).
- `snippets/s5.py` — subscribe to `{{ channels.traffic_signal_measurement }}` (DATEX-II 2017 profile).
- `snippets/s6.py` — subscribe to `{{ channels.transport_link_measurement }}` and dispatch on the SCOOT/GPS/ANPR `kind` discriminator (F6).
- `snippets/s7.py` — consume the static network topology across `network.{node,link,zone,path,turn}` and build an in-memory dict.

## Setup

```bash
uv venv && source .venv/bin/activate
uv pip install python-qpid-proton pydantic
```

## Run

Set `TOPAS_AMQP_URL` to your broker (defaults to
`amqps://localhost:5671`). For local development against an Apache
ActiveMQ Artemis broker:

```bash
export TOPAS_AMQP_URL=amqps://localhost:5671
python snippets/s1.py
```

`s3.py` additionally honours `TOPAS_ORIGINATOR` for the
`{{ headers.originator }}` AMQP application property.

## Don't hand-edit

The contents of `sdk/` and `snippets/` are generated by
`asyncapi_clients/generator/generate.py`. Re-run with
`make asyncapi-clients` after changing `asyncapi.yaml` or any
template under `asyncapi_clients/templates/python/`.
